    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Essential uses of «können»",
     "texto": [
      "The modal verb **können** has two main functions in German:",
      "1. **Learned abilities and skills:**",
      "It's the same as English «can» for abilities:",
      "**Ich kann schwimmen.** (I can swim).",
      "**Er kann sehr gut kochen.** (He can cook very well).",
      "**Sie kann gut tanzen.** (She can dance well).",
      "2. **Possibilities and polite requests:**",
      "**Kannst du mir helfen?** (Can you help me?).",
      "**Wir können heute zusammen lernen.** (We can study together today).",
      "**Sentence rule:** The modal is conjugated in **second position** and the infinitive of the action always goes to the **very end** of the sentence. In yes/no questions, the modal starts the sentence: **Kannst du Deutsch sprechen?**."
     ],
